---
description: Keep product value in the API; dashboard, widget and mobile stay thin clients
alwaysApply: true
---

# Backend is the backbone

The dashboard, chat widget and mobile app render, collect input and navigate. Product behavior lives in `apps/api`. A competitor who reads the JS bundle or a list response should see outcomes and labels, not the recipe.

## Value stays server-side

Prompts, playbook step goals, scoring, routing, autonomy resolution, model backing, tool policy, ticket transitions, inbox view membership and inbox-rule promotion. Clients receive the result and the fields a screen needs to draw it.

## Do

- One API operation per operator action (close, ask, assign, file a ticket). The server owns the order of steps.
- Add the service in `apps/api` first, then a thin call from the client.
- List and visitor surfaces return display fields. `system_prompt`, step goals, tool input/output and thinking traces belong on an explicit edit screen or an operator-only channel.
- Duplicate a rule in the client only as immediate feedback, and only when the server enforces the same rule and rejects the invalid state.
- Streaming is transport. The client attaches to the session the server named; it does not decide floor, session start or soft yes/no.

## Do not

- Chain several API calls in a page or hook to encode a business process.
- Copy thresholds, channel sets, stage graphs, slug tables or policy defaults into the bundle so they stay in sync with the API.
- Return edit-only fields on a list, picker, marketplace or widget payload.
- Put proprietary logic in `apps/dashboard/src/lib` (or the widget) that the API must mirror.

## Allowed in the client

- Layout, formatting, i18n, local preferences, accessibility.
- Optimistic UI the server can reject.
- Input checks that match a server rule, for instant feedback only.

## Anti-patterns

- Comments such as "Mirrors the API" next to a second copy of a predicate.
- Hardcoded policy numbers used when the API omits a field.
- A GET list that includes `system_prompt` or step goals because one edit screen also reads that endpoint.

## Still client-side (do not extend)

`thread-live.ts` list predicates, AI-handling default thresholds, managed model slug aliases, and composer `/ticket` / `/assign` matching. Move these to the API when you touch them. Do not add a third copy.
